[1m[38;5;231mHow long should the stored user identity survive?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153msessionStorage (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mSurvives reloads, clears when the tab closes. Cross-app within a session, no logout/expiry design needed yet.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m localStorage
     [38;5;246mSurvives browser restart until cleared. True 'stay logged in', but needs a logout path and accepts XSS exposure.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Cookie
     [38;5;246mPersists and is sent to the backend automatically. Right choice only if server-side code needs to read it.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m In-memory only
     [38;5;246mA shared module variable. Simplest and leaks nothing to disk, but does not survive a page reload.[39m
  [38;5;246m5. Type something.[39m
